{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Two-site sl(3) Gaudin: exact chain-side reference for the untwisting limit (W4, 2026-10-16)\n\nImplements `Gaudin-untwisted-exact-spec.md` (Tasks E1-E6). Exact rational / quadratic-surd algebra throughout (no numerical approximations; `N[]` only to choose a sign or to print gaps). Representations: Lambda in {[2,1,0] (adjoint, complete), [1,1,0], [2,2,0], [3,1,0], [3,2,0], [4,1,0]} on both sites.\n\n**Notebook state**: no native outputs are stored. The notebook was built by a script from the cell sources, each code cell's exact saved source was evaluated in the shared kernel K1 (cells in the order below, from a fresh kernel; Wolfram `Get` of the identical source text), and the printed `Grid` is stored in the markdown cell below the code cell as a table (not a native notebook output). Rerun in VS Code to store native outputs. The perturbation-theory cells (E4/E5) are specific to the adjoint (64 states); everything else loops over the six representations.\n\n**Conventions** (same as the round 1-3 chain notebooks `Gaudin-L2-chain*.wb`): plain non-Hermitian GT generators E_ij (i < j raising), site basis in the notebook `ps` order with the highest-weight pattern first, two-site product index (i-1)*dim + j, invariant diagonal metric G (E_ij^T G = G E_ji), Lax matrix L_ij(u) = g_ij + E1_ij/(u - theta_1) + E2_ij/(u - theta_2), S_k = coefficients of the column determinant cdet(dd - L) = dd^3 - S1 dd^2 + S2 dd - S3, S2 = e2(g) + Sum_s [H_s/(u - theta_s) + c2/(u - theta_s)^2], S3 = e3(g) + Sum_s [b_s/(u - theta_s) + a_s/(u - theta_s)^2], c2 = lam2 (lam1 + 1). Untwisted: g = 0. Twisted regime: g = diag(zeta), zeta = eps phi. theta = (2/7, -3/5) (theta12 = 31/35) unless stated; every Laurent datum carries the exact theta12-scaling H = eta/theta12, a = alpha/theta12, b = beta/theta12^2 at zeta = 0 (checked at three theta points), and H^(n), a^(n) ~ theta12^(n-1), b^(n) ~ theta12^(n-2) for the epsilon series (checked against theta = (1,0)).\n\nScratch note for readers: every helper that writes the tables (`wMd`, `runCell`) lives outside the notebook; the cells themselves only use their own definitions. The data-file path `refDir` is set in the cell of section E1 (cont.).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Setup: generators, metric, Lax matrix, S2/S3 (per-rep structural checks)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* fresh kernel state; Quiet because the front-end wrapper symbol ClearGlobals is Protected *)\nQuiet[ClearAll[\"Global`*\"]];\n(* GT basis and gl(3) generators: plain, non-Hermitian, exact rationals (same JJ as the round 1-3 chain notebooks); E_ij raises the weight for i < j, site basis ordered with the highest-weight pattern FIRST *)\nps[rep_] := ps[rep] = Block[{res = (Prepend[rep, #1] &) /@ Tuples[Table[Range[rep[[1, i + 1]], rep[[1, i]]], {i, 1, Length[rep[[1]]] - 1}]]}, If[Length[res[[1, 1]]] == 1, Reverse[Sort[res]], Reverse[Sort[Flatten[ps /@ res, 1]]]]];\ndimOf[rep_] := dimOf[rep] = Length[ps[{rep}]];\nJ0[k_][pat_] := J0[k][pat] = Sum[pat[[k, i]], {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat[[k - 1, i]], {i, 1, k - 1}];\nJp[k_][pat_] := Jp[k][pat] = -Sum[(Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k + 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}])*v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] + 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJm[k_][pat_] := Jm[k][pat] = Sum[(Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k - 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}])*v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] - 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJJ[k_, l_, rep_] := JJ[k, l, rep] = Which[\n  k == l, DiagonalMatrix[J0[k] /@ ps[{rep}]],\n  l == k + 1, Transpose[Table[(Coefficient[Jp[k][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#1]] &) /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n  l == k - 1, Transpose[Table[(Coefficient[Jm[l][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#1]] &) /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n  l > k + 1, JJ[k, k + 1, rep] . JJ[k + 1, l, rep] - JJ[k + 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k + 1, rep],\n  l < k - 1, JJ[k, k - 1, rep] . JJ[k - 1, l, rep] - JJ[k - 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k - 1, rep]];\nchecks = <||>; tims = <||>;\nzeroQ[a_] := Union[Flatten[Normal[a]]] === {0};\n(* the six representations of the round; the adjoint is first and is the only one used for the perturbation theory *)\nrepList = {{2, 1, 0}, {1, 1, 0}, {2, 2, 0}, {3, 1, 0}, {3, 2, 0}, {4, 1, 0}};\n(* build[Lam]: one Association per rep with the sparse generators of the two-site chain (site-1 index slow, site-2 index fast: KroneckerProduct order),\n   the one-site metric (diagonal G with G[[1]] = 1, Ee[i,j]^T G = G Ee[j,i]), total weights per product state *)\nbuild[Lam_] := build[Lam] = Module[{d1, d2, id1, Ee, E1, E2, wtL1, wtB, gv, gsol, gd},\n  d1 = dimOf[Lam]; d2 = d1^2; id1 = IdentityMatrix[d1, SparseArray];\n  Ee = Table[SparseArray[JJ[i, j, Lam]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\n  E1 = Table[KroneckerProduct[Ee[[i, j]], id1], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\n  E2 = Table[KroneckerProduct[id1, Ee[[i, j]]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\n  wtL1 = Table[Table[J0[k][p], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Lam}]}];\n  wtB = Flatten[Table[wtL1[[i]] + wtL1[[j]], {i, d1}, {j, d1}], 1];\n  gv = Array[gg, d1];\n  gsol = Solve[Flatten[Append[Table[Transpose[Normal[Ee[[i, j]]]] . DiagonalMatrix[gv] - DiagonalMatrix[gv] . Normal[Ee[[j, i]]], {i, 3}, {j, i + 1, 3}], {gv[[1]] - 1}]] == 0, gv];\n  gd = gv /. First[gsol];\n  <|\"Lam\" -> Lam, \"d1\" -> d1, \"d2\" -> d2, \"id2\" -> IdentityMatrix[d2, SparseArray], \"Ee\" -> Ee, \"E1\" -> E1, \"E2\" -> E2, \"wtL1\" -> wtL1, \"wtB\" -> wtB, \"g1\" -> gd, \"gd2\" -> Flatten[KroneckerProduct[gd, gd]], \"gsolN\" -> Length[gsol], \"nilp\" -> Lam[[1]] - Lam[[3]], \"lamTot\" -> Total[Lam]|>];\n(* the Lax matrix at zeta = 0 (or any twist g): L_ij(u) = g_ij + E1_ij/(u-th1) + E2_ij/(u-th2); S_k from the column determinant cdet(dd - L), normal ordered once (round 1, Task 0) *)\nLm[R_, g_, ths_, u_] := Association[Flatten[Table[{l[i, j] -> g[[i, j]] R[\"id2\"] + R[\"E1\"][[i, j]]/(u - ths[[1]]) + R[\"E2\"][[i, j]]/(u - ths[[2]]), lp[i, j] -> -R[\"E1\"][[i, j]]/(u - ths[[1]])^2 - R[\"E2\"][[i, j]]/(u - ths[[2]])^2, lpp[i, j] -> 2 R[\"E1\"][[i, j]]/(u - ths[[1]])^3 + 2 R[\"E2\"][[i, j]]/(u - ths[[2]])^3}, {i, 3}, {j, 3}], 1]];\n(* S2 and S3 as lists {coefficient, word} (word = product order), from the round-1 normal ordering of cdet *)\nSsym2 = {{-1, {lp[2, 2]}}, {-2, {lp[3, 3]}}, {1, {l[1, 1], l[2, 2]}}, {1, {l[1, 1], l[3, 3]}}, {-1, {l[2, 1], l[1, 2]}}, {1, {l[2, 2], l[3, 3]}}, {-1, {l[3, 1], l[1, 3]}}, {-1, {l[3, 2], l[2, 3]}}};\nSsym3 = {{1, {lpp[3, 3]}}, {-1, {l[1, 1], lp[3, 3]}}, {-1, {l[2, 2], lp[3, 3]}}, {1, {l[3, 1], lp[1, 3]}}, {1, {l[3, 2], lp[2, 3]}}, {-1, {lp[2, 2], l[3, 3]}}, {1, {lp[3, 2], l[2, 3]}}, {1, {l[1, 1], l[2, 2], l[3, 3]}}, {-1, {l[1, 1], l[3, 2], l[2, 3]}}, {-1, {l[2, 1], l[1, 2], l[3, 3]}}, {1, {l[2, 1], l[3, 2], l[1, 3]}}, {1, {l[3, 1], l[1, 2], l[2, 3]}}, {-1, {l[3, 1], l[2, 2], l[1, 3]}}};\nSk[R_, 1, g_, ths_, u_] := (Total[Diagonal[g]] + R[\"lamTot\"] (1/(u - ths[[1]]) + 1/(u - ths[[2]]))) R[\"id2\"];\nSk[R_, k_, g_, ths_, u_] := Module[{M = Lm[R, g, ths, u]}, Total[Table[t[[1]] If[t[[2]] === {}, R[\"id2\"], Dot @@ Map[M[#] &, t[[2]]]], {t, If[k == 2, Ssym2, Ssym3]}]]];\n(* per-rep structural checks: gl(3) relations, G invariant, nilpotency of E_ij^(nilp+1), the Gaudin family commutes, S1 is the scalar |Lam| sum 1/(u-th) *)\nDo[Module[{R = build[Lam], Ee, comm, nilp, g0, thT = {2/7, -3/5}, gZ, pts = {3/7, -2/9, 5/11}, t0},\n  t0 = AbsoluteTime[]; Ee = R[\"Ee\"]; nilp = R[\"nilp\"];\n  comm = Flatten[Table[Normal[Ee[[i, j]] . Ee[[k, l]] - Ee[[k, l]] . Ee[[i, j]] - (KroneckerDelta[j, k] Ee[[i, l]] - KroneckerDelta[l, i] Ee[[k, j]])], {i, 3}, {j, 3}, {k, 3}, {l, 3}]];\n  gZ = DiagonalMatrix[{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}];\n  checks[{Lam, \"gl3 relations\"}] = Union[comm] === {0};\n  checks[{Lam, \"G positive invariant unique\"}] = R[\"gsolN\"] == 1 && And @@ Positive[R[\"g1\"]] && And @@ Flatten[Table[Transpose[Normal[Ee[[i, j]]]] . DiagonalMatrix[R[\"g1\"]] === DiagonalMatrix[R[\"g1\"]] . Normal[Ee[[j, i]]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\n  checks[{Lam, \"nilpotency\"}] = And @@ Flatten[Table[If[i == j, True, Max[Abs[Normal[MatrixPower[Ee[[i, j]], nilp + 1]]]] == 0], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]] && Max[Abs[Normal[MatrixPower[Ee[[1, 3]], nilp]]]] != 0;\n  If[R[\"d2\"] <= 225, checks[{Lam, \"[S_a(u),S_b(v)]=0 (twisted, 3 pairs)\"}] = Table[zeroQ[Sk[R, a, gZ, thT, pts[[1]]] . Sk[R, b, gZ, thT, pts[[2]]] - Sk[R, b, gZ, thT, pts[[2]]] . Sk[R, a, gZ, thT, pts[[1]]]], {a, 2, 3}, {b, a, 3}]];\n  checks[{Lam, \"time\"}] = ToString[Round[1000 (AbsoluteTime[] - t0)]] <> \" ms\"], {Lam, repList}];\nGrid[Join[{{\"rep\", \"dim, dim^2, distinct total weights, G diagonal\"}}, Table[{ToString[Lam, InputForm], ToString[{build[Lam][\"d1\"], build[Lam][\"d2\"], Length[Union[build[Lam][\"wtB\"]]], build[Lam][\"g1\"]}, InputForm]}, {Lam, repList}], List @@@ Normal[checks]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
