  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## E1 (cont.). Universal copies in multiplicity-2 sectors, CG tables, and the data files `ref/untwisted-exact-<l1><l2><l3>.txt` (part 1)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* E1 (cont.) + data files. HW branches = (sector mu, copy): for multiplicity 1 the HW ket; for multiplicity 2 the two UNIVERSAL copies = eigenvectors of S3c[1,2] on the HW space (round 2/3): 2x2 matrix A1 = theta12*a_1 (theta-independent, section E2), quadratic lambda^2 - tr lambda + det = 0, eigenvalues lambda = (tr -+ f Sqrt[D0])/2 (D0 squarefree integer), eigenvector c = (A1[1,2], lambda - A1[1,1]) (A1.c = lambda c, in the canonical HW basis hwK), copy 1 = smaller eigenvalue. All other Laurent matrices commute with A1 (checked) so each is x0 + x1*A1 and takes the value x0 + x1*lambda on a copy. Vectors are written as pairs (vA, vB) of rational vectors meaning vA + Sqrt[D0] vB (no Sqrt in the file); the exact G-norm^2 is a pair too. Sign convention: first nonzero GT component (product-basis order) is positive. *)\nck = <||>;\nrefDir = \"C:/Users/pryan/git-projects/gaudin-cg/Paul/Mathematica/Gaudin/ref/\";\nsqfreeSplit[x_] := Module[{n = Numerator[x] Denominator[x], f, sq, kk}, f = FactorInteger[n]; sq = Times @@ (#[[1]]^Mod[#[[2]], 2] & /@ f); kk = Sqrt[n/sq]; {sq, kk/Denominator[x]}];\nqval[x0_, x1_, lam_] := {x0 + x1 lam[[1]], x1 lam[[2]]};\nbranchData[Lam_, mu_] := Module[{R = build[Lam], ld = lauData[{Lam, mu}], m, kets},\n  m = ld[\"mult\"]; kets = embed[Lam, mu, #] & /@ hwK[Lam, mu];\n  If[m == 1,\n   {<|\"copy\" -> 1, \"D0\" -> 0, \"vA\" -> kets[[1]], \"vB\" -> ConstantArray[0, R[\"d2\"]], \"gn\" -> {gNorm2[Lam, kets[[1]]], 0},\n     \"eta\" -> {{ld[\"eta\"][[1, 1, 1]], 0}, {ld[\"eta\"][[2, 1, 1]], 0}}, \"alpha\" -> {{ld[\"A\"][[1, 1, 1]], 0}, {ld[\"A\"][[2, 1, 1]], 0}}, \"beta\" -> {{ld[\"B\"][[1, 1, 1]], 0}, {ld[\"B\"][[2, 1, 1]], 0}}|>},\n   Module[{A1 = ld[\"A\"][[1]], trA, detA, disc, f, D0, lams},\n    trA = Tr[A1]; detA = Det[A1]; disc = trA^2 - 4 detA; {D0, f} = sqfreeSplit[disc];\n    lams = {{trA/2, -f/2}, {trA/2, f/2}};\n    Table[Module[{lam = lams[[ic]], cA, cB, vA, vB, num, sgn, x1, ev, c2n},\n      cA = {A1[[1, 2]], lam[[1]] - A1[[1, 1]]}; cB = {0, lam[[2]]};\n      c2n = LCM @@ Denominator[Join[cA, cB]]; cA = c2n cA; cB = c2n cB;\n      vA = cA . kets; vB = cB . kets;\n      num = N[vA + Sqrt[D0] vB, 30]; sgn = Sign[First[Select[num, Abs[#] > 10^-20 &]]];\n      vA = sgn vA; vB = sgn vB;\n      x1[X_] := X[[1, 2]]/A1[[1, 2]];\n      ev[X_] := qval[X[[1, 1]] - x1[X] A1[[1, 1]], x1[X], lam];\n      <|\"copy\" -> ic, \"D0\" -> D0, \"vA\" -> vA, \"vB\" -> vB, \"gn\" -> {Total[R[\"gd2\"] (vA^2 + D0 vB^2)], Total[R[\"gd2\"] 2 vA vB]},\n        \"eta\" -> {{ld[\"eta\"][[1, 1, 1]], 0}, {ld[\"eta\"][[2, 1, 1]], 0}}, \"alpha\" -> {ev[ld[\"A\"][[1]]], ev[ld[\"A\"][[2]]]}, \"beta\" -> {ev[ld[\"B\"][[1]]], ev[ld[\"B\"][[2]]]},\n        \"lam\" -> lam|>], {ic, 2}]]]];\ncommuteQ[ld_] := And @@ Flatten[Table[ld[a][[s]] . ld[b][[t]] === ld[b][[t]] . ld[a][[s]], {a, {\"A\", \"B\"}}, {b, {\"A\", \"B\"}}, {s, 2}, {t, 2}]];\n(* copies: G-orthogonal in Q(Sqrt[D0]); all four Laurent matrices commute; the copy is an exact eigenvector of A1: A1.c = lambda c is built in, so test the eigen-equation of the FULL operator via the alpha value *)\ncheckCopies[Lam_, mu_] := Module[{ld = lauData[{Lam, mu}], bd = branchData[Lam, mu], R = build[Lam], D0, v1, v2, g = build[Lam][\"gd2\"], r0, r1},\n  If[ld[\"mult\"] == 1, True,\n   D0 = bd[[1, \"D0\"]]; v1 = bd[[1]]; v2 = bd[[2]];\n   r0 = Total[g (v1[\"vA\"] v2[\"vA\"] + D0 v1[\"vB\"] v2[\"vB\"])]; r1 = Total[g (v1[\"vA\"] v2[\"vB\"] + v1[\"vB\"] v2[\"vA\"])];\n   {r0 == 0 && r1 == 0, commuteQ[ld]}]];\nsparsePairs[vA_, vB_] := Table[{i, vA[[i]], vB[[i]]}, {i, Select[Range[Length[vA]], vA[[#]] != 0 || vB[[#]] != 0 &]}];\nfmt[x_] := StringReplace[ToString[x, InputForm, PageWidth -> Infinity], {\"\\n\" -> \"\", \" \" -> \"\"}];\nwriteRepFile[Lam_] := Module[{R = build[Lam], d1 = build[Lam][\"d1\"], lines = {}, th = {2/7, -3/5}, secs = hwSecsOf[Lam], add},\n  add[tag_, args__] := AppendTo[lines, StringRiffle[Prepend[fmt /@ {args}, tag], \"\\t\"]];\n  lines = {\n   \"# untwisted-exact-\" <> StringJoin[ToString /@ Lam] <> \".txt   (agent W4, notebook Paul/Mathematica/Gaudin/Experiments/Gaudin-untwisted-exact.wb, 2026-10-16)\",\n   \"# Two-site gl(3) Gaudin chain, Lambda = \" <> fmt[Lam] <> \" on both sites, UNTWISTED (zeta = 0). All numbers exact: integers, rationals p/q (Wolfram InputForm), no Sqrt anywhere.\",\n   \"# FORMAT: one record per line, TAB-separated fields; the first field is the tag; every other field is a Wolfram InputForm expression (nested braces = lists, p/q = rational) without spaces. Lines starting with # are comments.\",\n   \"# GT basis (one site): the notebook ps[{Lambda}] order = Reverse[Sort[Gelfand-Tsetlin patterns]]; index 1 is the highest-weight pattern. Record GTBASIS lists the patterns {{l1,l2,l3},{m1,m2},{k}}; WEIGHTS1 the one-site weight (E11,E22,E33 eigenvalues) per index; GMET1 the invariant diagonal metric G (G[[1]]=1; E_ij^T G = G E_ji, the GT matrices are NOT Hermitian).\",\n   \"# Two-site product basis: index (i,j) -> (i-1)*DIM + j, i = site-1 GT index (slow), j = site-2 index (fast); site 2 = highest weight is j = 1. Generators are the plain GT matrices (E_ij, i<j raising); inner product <a,b>_G = Sum g_i g_j a b.\",\n   \"# Laurent data convention: S2 = Sum_s [H_s/(u-th_s) + c2/(u-th_s)^2], S3 = Sum_s [b_s/(u-th_s) + a_s/(u-th_s)^2] (untwisted: no constant, no triple pole), c2 = lam2(lam1+1). Scaling: H_s = eta_s/th12, a_s = alpha_s/th12, b_s = beta_s/th12^2, th12 = th1 - th2, with eta, alpha, beta theta-independent (verified at three theta points). THETA below is the reference point th = (2/7,-3/5), th12 = 31/35.\",\n   \"# Pair notation (x0,x1) = x0 + x1*Sqrt[D0] (D0 squarefree integer; D0 = 0 means rational, x1 = 0).\",\n   \"# RECORDS: REP {l1,l2,l3} | DIM | GTBASIS | WEIGHTS1 | GMET1 | THETA | NSECTORS | CAS1 cas2(Lam) cas3(Lam) | SECTOR mu mult wspace-dim dimV_mu cas2(mu) cas3(mu) |\",\n   \"#   HWBASIS mu k {{idx,val},...} (canonical rational HW kets = primitive integer vectors, RowReduce order; k = 1..mult) | GRAM mu {{..}} (exact G Gram matrix of the HWBASIS kets) | LAURMAT mu A1 A2 B1 B2 eta1 (theta12-scaled m x m matrices acting as X.H = H.M on the HWBASIS kets: column j = image of ket j) |\",\n   \"#   BRANCH mu copy D0 vec gnorm2 cg eta alpha beta :  vec = {{idx,vA,vB},...} nonzero entries of the HW vector vA + Sqrt[D0]*vB (unnormalised, first nonzero component positive); gnorm2 = pair (exact G-norm^2); cg = {{nu,cA,cB},...} the site-1 GT index nu slice of the vector at site-2 index 1, i.e. the unnormalised CG coefficients <e_nu (x) e_1|Psi0>; normalised C_nu = (cA + Sqrt[D0] cB)/Sqrt[gnorm2];\",\n   \"#   eta, alpha, beta = {pair for s=1, pair for s=2} theta12-scaled Laurent data of the branch; branch copies in a multiplicity-2 sector are the eigenvectors of S3c[1,2] (copy 1 = smaller alpha_1).\"};\n  add[\"REP\", Lam]; add[\"DIM\", d1]; add[\"GTBASIS\", ps[{Lam}]]; add[\"WEIGHTS1\", R[\"wtL1\"]]; add[\"GMET1\", R[\"g1\"]]; add[\"THETA\", th]; add[\"NSECTORS\", Length[secs]];\n  add[\"CAS1\", cas1[R, 2], cas1[R, 3]];\n  Do[Module[{ld = lauData[{Lam, mu}], hs = hwK[Lam, mu], bd = branchData[Lam, mu], kets},\n    kets = embed[Lam, mu, #] & /@ hs;\n    add[\"SECTOR\", mu, ld[\"mult\"], Length[secOf[Lam, mu]], weylDim[mu], ld[\"cas2\"], ld[\"cas3\"]];\n    Do[add[\"HWBASIS\", mu, k, sparsePairs[kets[[k]], 0 kets[[k]]][[All, {1, 2}]]], {k, Length[hs]}];\n    add[\"GRAM\", mu, gGram[Lam, mu]];\n    add[\"LAURMAT\", mu, ld[\"A\"][[1]], ld[\"A\"][[2]], ld[\"B\"][[1]], ld[\"B\"][[2]], ld[\"eta\"][[1]]];\n    Do[Module[{b = bd[[ic]], cgA, cgB},\n      cgA = cgSlice[Lam, b[\"vA\"]]; cgB = cgSlice[Lam, b[\"vB\"]];\n      add[\"BRANCH\", mu, ic, b[\"D0\"], sparsePairs[b[\"vA\"], b[\"vB\"]], b[\"gn\"], sparsePairs[cgA, cgB], b[\"eta\"], b[\"alpha\"], b[\"beta\"]]], {ic, Length[bd]}]], {mu, secs}];\n  Export[refDir <> \"untwisted-exact-\" <> StringJoin[ToString /@ Lam] <> \".txt\", StringRiffle[lines, \"\\n\"] <> \"\\n\", \"Text\"]; Length[lines]];\nnlines = <||>;\nDo[ck[{Lam, \"mult-2 copies: {G-orthogonal, all Laurent matrices commute}\"}] = Table[checkCopies[Lam, mu], {mu, hwSecsOf[Lam]}];\n  nlines[Lam] = writeRepFile[Lam], {Lam, repList}];\ntab = Flatten[Table[Table[With[{bd = branchData[Lam, mu], ld = lauData[{Lam, mu}]}, {ToString[Lam, InputForm], ToString[mu, InputForm], ld[\"mult\"], ToString[bd[[1, \"D0\"]], InputForm], ToString[Table[{b[\"copy\"], b[\"gn\"], b[\"alpha\"], b[\"beta\"]}, {b, bd}], InputForm]}], {mu, Select[hwSecsOf[Lam], lauData[{Lam, #}][\"mult\"] == 2 &]}], {Lam, repList}], 1];\n(* CG tables of the adjoint: C_nu = (cA + Sqrt[D0] cB)/Sqrt[gnorm2] = <e_nu (x) e_1|Psi_0>/||Psi_0||_G, nu = site-1 GT index *)\ntabCG = Flatten[Table[Table[With[{b = bd, mu = mu}, {\"CG \" <> ToString[mu, InputForm] <> \" copy \" <> ToString[b[\"copy\"]], ToString[b[\"D0\"]], ToString[Table[{nu, cgSlice[{2, 1, 0}, b[\"vA\"]][[nu]], cgSlice[{2, 1, 0}, b[\"vB\"]][[nu]]}, {nu, Select[Range[8], cgSlice[{2, 1, 0}, b[\"vA\"]][[#]] != 0 || cgSlice[{2, 1, 0}, b[\"vB\"]][[#]] != 0 &]}], InputForm], ToString[b[\"gn\"], InputForm]}], {bd, branchData[{2, 1, 0}, mu]}], {mu, hwSecsOf[{2, 1, 0}]}], 1];\nchecks = Join[checks, ck];\nGrid[Join[{{\"files written (lines)\", ToString[nlines, InputForm]}}, {{\"adjoint CG tables: branch\", \"D0\", \"{nu, cA, cB} (unnormalised slice cA + Sqrt[D0] cB)\", \"G-norm^2 pair (n0, n1): n0 + n1 Sqrt[D0]\"}}, tabCG, {{\"Lam\", \"mu\", \"mult\", \"D0\", \"{copy, G-norm^2 pair, alpha pairs (s=1,2), beta pairs}\"}}, tab, List @@@ Normal[ck] /. {a_, b_} :> {a, b}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
