   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* E3 (cont.). General 3F2 test. A third-order Fuchsian equation on three singular points is a 3F2 equation (up to a Moebius map and a gauge x^e0 (1-x)^e1) iff after the gauge the exponents at the point mapped to s = 1 are {0, 1, sigma}, i.e. that point carries a CONSECUTIVE PAIR of exponents; the equation is then fixed by the exponents at s = 0 ({0, 1-b1, 1-b2}) and at s = infinity (a1, a2, a3). The test below tries every role assignment (which singular point of {0, 1, infinity} becomes s = 0, 1, infinity), every choice of the exponent set element normalised to 0 at s = 0 and every consecutive pair at s = 1, transforms D0 exactly and compares coefficient-by-coefficient with the 3F2 operator. Exponents: at 0 and 1 the list of the cell above, at infinity Riemann exponents -d. *)\nck = <||>;\nmobTab = <|{0, 1, Infinity} -> Function[x, x], {1, 0, Infinity} -> Function[x, 1 - x], {0, Infinity, 1} -> Function[x, x/(x - 1)], {Infinity, 0, 1} -> Function[x, 1/(1 - x)], {1, Infinity, 0} -> Function[x, (x - 1)/x], {Infinity, 1, 0} -> Function[x, 1/x]|>;\nmobInv = <|{0, 1, Infinity} -> Function[s, s], {1, 0, Infinity} -> Function[s, 1 - s], {0, Infinity, 1} -> Function[s, s/(s - 1)], {Infinity, 0, 1} -> Function[s, 1 - 1/s], {1, Infinity, 0} -> Function[s, 1/(1 - s)], {Infinity, 1, 0} -> Function[s, 1/s]|>;\nhypCoeffs2[aa_, bb_, s_] := Module[{f, th, p1, p2, p3, q1, q2, q3, hop},\n  th[g_, c_] := s D[g, s] + c g;\n  p1 = th[f[s], 0]; p2 = th[p1, bb[[2]] - 1]; p3 = th[p2, bb[[1]] - 1];\n  q1 = th[f[s], aa[[3]]]; q2 = th[q1, aa[[2]]]; q3 = th[q2, aa[[1]]];\n  hop = Expand[p3 - s q3];\n  Table[Simplify[Coefficient[hop, D[f[s], {s, k}]]], {k, 3, 0, -1}]];\nhypGeneral[dat_, ind_] := Module[{S = sfun[dat], expo, wit = {}, xE3 = Symbol[\"xE3\"], sE3 = Symbol[\"sE3\"], w},\n  expo = <|0 -> ind[\"fin\"], 1 -> ind[\"fin\"], Infinity -> -ind[\"inf\"]|>;\n  Do[Module[{pZ = roles[[1]], pO = roles[[2]], pI = roles[[3]]},\n    Do[Module[{c = pair[[1]], taus, eZ, e0, e1, exZ, exO, exI, g, m, mi, ex, cs, aaP, bbP, cH, cT, tau},\n       tau = <|pO -> -c|>;\n       Do[\n        tau[pZ] = -rz; tau[pI] = -(tau[pZ] + tau[pO]);\n        e0 = -tau[0]; e1 = -tau[1];\n        exZ = Sort[expo[pZ] + tau[pZ]]; exO = Sort[expo[pO] + tau[pO]]; exI = Sort[expo[pI] + tau[pI]];\n        If[MemberQ[exO, 0] && MemberQ[exO, 1] && MemberQ[exZ, 0],\n         Module[{bsP, w1, rest},\n          bbP = 1 - Delete[exZ, First@Flatten[Position[exZ, 0]]];\n          aaP = exI;\n          g = xE3^e0 (1 - xE3)^e1; m = mobTab[roles]; mi = mobInv[roles];\n          ex = Expand[(D[g w[m[xE3]], {xE3, 3}] - S[[1]][xE3] D[g w[m[xE3]], {xE3, 2}] + S[[2]][xE3] D[g w[m[xE3]], xE3] - S[[3]][xE3] g w[m[xE3]])/g /. Derivative[k_][w][_] :> W[k] /. w[_] :> W[0]];\n          cs = Table[Coefficient[ex, W[k]], {k, 3, 0, -1}];\n          cs = Together[cs /. xE3 -> mi[sE3]];\n          cH = hypCoeffs2[aaP, bbP, sE3];\n          If[Together[cs - cH Together[cs[[1]]/cH[[1]]]] === {0, 0, 0, 0}, AppendTo[wit, <|\"roles\" -> roles, \"a\" -> aaP, \"b\" -> bbP, \"gauge\" -> {e0, e1}|>]]]],\n        {rz, expo[pZ]}]],\n      {pair, Select[Subsets[expo[pO], {2}] // Map[Sort], #[[2]] - #[[1]] == 1 &]}]],\n   {roles, Keys[mobTab]}];\n  wit];\nbranchesAll = Flatten[Table[Table[{Lam, mu, ic}, {ic, lauData[{Lam, mu}][\"mult\"]}], {Lam, repList}, {mu, hwSecsOf[Lam]}], 2];\ntab = {};\nDo[Module[{Lam = b[[1]], mu = b[[2]], ic = b[[3]], dat, ind, anyPair, wit, t0 = AbsoluteTime[]},\n  dat = odeData[Lam, mu, ic]; ind = indData[dat];\n  anyPair = Or @@ (MatchQ[Differences[Sort[#]], {___, 1, ___}] & /@ {ind[\"fin\"], -ind[\"inf\"]});\n  wit = If[anyPair, hypGeneral[dat, ind], {}];\n  AppendTo[tab, {ToString[Lam, InputForm], ToString[mu, InputForm], ic, ToString[anyPair], ToString[Length[wit] > 0], ToString[If[wit === {}, \"-\", First[wit]], InputForm], ToString[Round[1000 (AbsoluteTime[] - t0)]] <> \" ms\"}]], {b, branchesAll}];\nck[\"number of branches that are 3F2 equations / that have a consecutive pair of exponents / total\"] = {Count[tab[[All, 5]], \"True\"], Count[tab[[All, 4]], \"True\"], Length[tab]};\nchecks = Join[checks, ck];\nGrid[Join[{{\"Lam\", \"mu\", \"copy\", \"consecutive pair of exponents at some singular point (0, 1: {0,l2+1,l1+2}; inf: {-d})\", \"oper is a 3F2 equation (exact operator identity after Moebius map + gauge)\", \"first witness: roles {s=0,s=1,s=inf} <- points, a_j, b_j, gauge (e0,e1)\", \"time\"}}, tab, List @@@ Normal[ck] /. {a_, c_} :> {a, ToString[c, InputForm], \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
