  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Untwisted sl(3) Gaudin: exact reference (2026-10-16)\n\nNotation: T = |Lambda|, theta12 = theta1 - theta2, c2 = lam2 (lam1 + 1), C2(l) = Sum_i l_i (l_i + 4 - 2i), C3(l) = l1^3 + l2^3 + l3^3 + 4 l1^2 + l2^2 - 2 l3^2 - l1 l2 - l1 l3 - l2 l3 + 4 l1 - 2 l2 - 2 l3 (C2 = Sum E_ik E_ki, C3 = Sum E_ij E_jk E_ki; exact on all 37 sectors and 6 one-site reps), mu = HW weight of the sector. Every statement below is an exact identity checked in this notebook unless marked.\n\n**E1, sectors and multiplicities (HW kets canonical, primitive integer vectors; dimension count and raising residual exact).** [2,1,0]: (4,2,0), (4,1,1), (3,3,0), (3,2,1) x2, (2,2,2). [1,1,0]: (2,2,0), (2,1,1). [2,2,0]: (4,4,0), (4,3,1), (4,2,2). [3,1,0]: (6,2,0), (6,1,1), (5,3,0), (5,2,1) x2, (4,4,0), (4,3,1) x2, (4,2,2), (3,3,2). [3,2,0]: (6,4,0), (6,3,1), (6,2,2), (5,5,0), (5,4,1) x2, (5,3,2) x2, (4,4,2), (4,3,3). [4,1,0]: (8,2,0), (8,1,1), (7,3,0), (7,2,1) x2, (6,4,0), (6,3,1) x2, (6,2,2), (5,5,0), (5,4,1) x2, (5,3,2), (4,4,2). Multiplicity <= 2 everywhere (45 HW branches in all). The two copies in a multiplicity-2 sector are the eigenvectors of the 2x2 matrix of S3c[1,2] = theta12 a_1 (theta-independent, rational), eigenvalues (tr -+ f Sqrt[D0])/2, copy 1 = smaller; they are G-orthogonal and all four Laurent matrices commute with it. CG tables C_nu = <e_nu (x) e_1|Psi_0>/||Psi_0||_G (adjoint: nu is the site-1 GT index; C_nu = slice/Sqrt[G-norm^2], both exact in the data files): (4,2,0): C_1 = 1; (4,1,1): C_2 = -1/Sqrt[2]; (3,3,0): C_3 = -1/Sqrt[2]; (2,2,2): C_8 = 2/Sqrt[288]; (3,2,1) copy 1: C_4 = (21 - 9 Sqrt[5])/Sqrt[7560 - 3240 Sqrt[5]], C_5 = (-3 + 3 Sqrt[5])/Sqrt[7560 - 3240 Sqrt[5]], copy 2 with Sqrt[5] -> -Sqrt[5].\n\n**E2, untwisted Laurent data (all exact; theta-scaling H = eta/theta12, a = alpha/theta12, b = beta/theta12^2 verified at three theta points).**\n- H_1 = -H_2 = eta/theta12 with eta = T^2 - (C2(mu) - 2 C2(Lambda))/2 (on all 37 sectors; = 4, 6, 6, 9, 12 for the adjoint (4,2,0), (4,1,1), (3,3,0), (3,2,1), (2,2,2)).\n- a_1 = -a_2 = alpha/theta12 with **alpha = [4 T (1+T)^2 - 3 (1+T) C2(mu) + C3(mu)]/6** (exact fit over the 30 multiplicity-1 sectors with 6 parameters, then verified on every sector; on multiplicity-2 sectors this is the mean of the two copies = tr A1/2). Consequences: alpha = 0 iff mu3 = 0; alpha = eta for mu3 > 0 except lam2 >= 2 where alpha - eta = 4 ([2,2,0] (4,2,2)), 6 ([3,2,0] (6,2,2)), 6 ((4,4,2)), 10 ((4,3,3)).\n- b_1 = -b_2 = beta/theta12^2; beta = 0 on every multiplicity-1 sector; on multiplicity 2 beta_1(copy) = alpha_1(copy)(eta - alpha_1(copy))/c2 (the no-log relation; holds on 7 of 8 multiplicity-2 sectors, fails only on [3,2,0] (5,3,2)); the two copies have alpha_pm = (tr -+ Sqrt[disc])/2 and beta = +-Sqrt[disc] with tr = eta + 2 c2, disc = eta^2 - 4 c2^2 on all multiplicity-2 sectors except [3,2,0] (5,3,2) (tr = 56 = eta + 2 c2 + 18, disc = 192, not 228). Adjoint (3,2,1): alpha_pm = (15 -+ 3 Sqrt[5])/2, beta = +-3 Sqrt[5], lambda^2 - 15 lambda + 45 = 0.\n- **Sum rules (exact matrix identities on every HW space, 37 sectors): b_1 + b_2 = 0 and a_1 + a_2 + theta1 b_1 + theta2 b_2 = 0**; so S3 = O(u^-3) and u = infinity is a regular singular point of the untwisted oper.\n\n**E3, the untwisted oper D0 = dd^3 - S1 dd^2 + S2 dd - S3 (45/45 branches).** Local exponents at theta_s: {0, lam2+1, lam1+2}; at infinity (y ~ u^d): **d = {mu1+2, mu2+1, mu3}** (indicial roots, all 45 branches); Fuchs relation: 2 Sum(finite exponents) - Sum(d) = 3 (all). The solution space of D0 is spanned by three polynomials of exact degrees d (apparent singularities at theta1, theta2): cumulative dimensions per degree 0..2 lam1+4 are in the table (e.g. adjoint (2,2,2): degrees 2,3,4; (4,2,0): 0,3,6). The twisted dual degrees mu_j are shifted by (2,1,0). The direct oper (Pi^p o adjoint o Pi^-p, p = lam1 - lam3) has polynomial solutions of degrees {2 lam1+2-mu3, 2 lam1+1-mu2, 2 lam1-mu1} on 43 of 45 branches (exceptions: [1,1,0] (2,2,0) gives {0,2,4}, [2,2,0] (4,4,0) gives {0,2,6}). **Hypergeometric verdict (exact operator comparison after a Moebius map and gauge, all role assignments): the oper is a 3F2 equation iff some singular point carries a consecutive pair of exponents, which happens on exactly 20 of the 45 branches**: lam1 = lam2 (consecutive pair {lam+1, lam+2} at theta_s: [1,1,0], [2,2,0], all 5 branches), or mu1 = mu2 or mu2 = mu3 (pair {-d_j} at infinity: adjoint (4,1,1), (3,3,0), (2,2,2); [3,1,0] (6,1,1), (4,4,0), (4,2,2), (3,3,2); [3,2,0] (6,2,2), (5,5,0), (4,4,2), (4,3,3); [4,1,0] (8,1,1), (6,2,2), (5,5,0), (4,4,2)); for these the parameters are b = (-lam2, -lam1-1) (witness roles: s=0 at theta2, s=1 at infinity, s=infinity at theta1, gauge (1-x)^(...); for lam1 = lam2: s=x, gauge (1-x)^(lam+1)), a_j = tabulated witness. On the other 25 branches (all with mu1 > mu2 > mu3 and lam1 != lam2, including every multiplicity-2 sector) there is no consecutive pair at any of the three points, hence no 3F2 form. No logs occur (all local exponents differ by integers, all solutions polynomial).\n\n**E4, degenerate perturbation theory (adjoint, zeta = eps phi, theta = (2/7,-3/5); exact Rayleigh-Schroedinger on the weight-mu space, isolating operator H_1 + a_1/7, all six Laurent operators commute and every series eigen-equation holds exactly).** Series to order 7 at phi = (1/3,-2/7,5/11) and phi' = (-2/5,3/8,7/11), symbolic phi to order 3, Psi_n to order 4 symbolically (E5). Exact: H_1 + H_2 = Sum_{i != j} phi_i mu_j (order 1 only), b_s = a_s (H_s - a_s)/3 order by order, theta12 scaling H^(n), a^(n) ~ theta12^(n-1), b^(n) ~ theta12^(n-2). First orders, theta12 = 31/35: H_1^(1) = phi1 + 2 phi2 + 3 phi3 ((4,2,0)); phi1 + (5/2)(phi2+phi3) ((4,1,1)); (3/2)(phi1+phi2) + 3 phi3 ((3,3,0)); 2(phi1+phi2+phi3) ((2,2,2)); octet copy 1: ((15+Sqrt[5])/10) phi1 + (2 - 1/Sqrt[5]) phi2 + ((25+Sqrt[5])/10) phi3 (copy 2: Sqrt[5] -> -Sqrt[5]); H_2^(1) = H_1^(1) on the four non-octet branches, and on the octets H_2^(1)(copy 1) = (3/2 - 1/(2Sqrt[5])) phi1 + (2 + 1/Sqrt[5]) phi2 + (5/2 - 1/(2Sqrt[5])) phi3; a_1^(1): 3 phi3, (3/2)(phi2+phi3), 3 phi3, phi1+phi2+phi3, octet ((3-Sqrt[5])/10) phi1 + (3(3-Sqrt[5])/10) phi2 + (9/5+2/Sqrt[5]) phi3; second orders: (4,2,0): H^(2) = a^(2) = 0 (b_1^(2) = phi3(phi1+2phi2)); (4,1,1): H_1^(2) = (theta12/8)(phi2-phi3)^2, a_1^(2) = (3 theta12/8)(phi2-phi3)^2; (3,3,0): H_1^(2) = (theta12/8)(phi1-phi2)^2, a^(2) = 0; (2,2,2): H_1^(2) = (theta12/6) Q, a_1^(2) = (theta12/4) Q with Q = phi1^2+phi2^2+phi3^2-phi1 phi2-phi1 phi3-phi2 phi3; octets and orders 3..7 are in the table. The top branch is exact: Psi_B = e1 (x) e1 for all eps (H_1 = 4/theta12 + eps(phi1+2phi2+3phi3), series terminate). **Psi_1 content** (Psi_B stays in the weight-mu space; decomposed into irreps nu >= mu by exact (C2,C3) projectors): (4,1,1): Psi_1 = (31/140)(phi3-phi2)(1,1) lies entirely in the (4,2,0) irrep (its G-norm^2 is (961/9800)(phi2-phi3)^2 = (theta12^2/8)(phi2-phi3)^2, Psi_0 = (1,-1) having G-norm^2 2); (3,3,0): same with phi2 - phi1, entirely in (4,2,0); (2,2,2): entirely in the (3,2,1) octet irrep, G-norm^2 = (15376/1225)Q, no (3,3,0), (4,1,1), (4,2,0) component; octets: components in all four irreps (3,2,1), (3,3,0), (4,1,1), (4,2,0), proportional to (phi2-phi3), (phi1-phi2) combinations (table). Orders 3..7: for (4,2,0) everything is zero beyond the stated polynomials; for (4,1,1), (3,3,0) and (2,2,2) H_1^(3) = H_1^(5) = 0 (and a_1^(3) = a_1^(5) = 0 for (4,1,1), (3,3,0), nonzero for (2,2,2)); the octets have all orders nonzero (exact p + q Sqrt[5] values in the table).\n\n**E5, leading orders in the regime.** x(zeta) is a homogeneous polynomial covector of degree lam2 (all six reps, exact; adjoint x = (z2-z1, z3-z1, z2-z1, 2z3-z1-z2, 3(z2-z1), 3(z3-z1), 2(z3-z2), 3(z3-z2)) exactly as in the plan; [1,1,0]: (z2-z1, z3-z1, z3-z2); [2,2,0]: ((z1-z2)^2, 2(z1-z2)(z1-z3), 2(z1-z3)^2, 2(z1-z2)(z2-z3), 4(z1-z3)(z2-z3), 4(z2-z3)^2); [3,1,0], [3,2,0], [4,1,0] in the data files). <x0^G|Psi_B> = eps^(2+k_B)(coef/Sqrt[gnorm0]) + ..., **k_B = 0, 1, 1, 2, 2, 4** for (4,2,0), (4,1,1), (3,3,0), (3,2,1)x2, (2,2,2), i.e. exponents 2, 3, 3, 4, 4, 6, with coefficient <x(phi)(x)x(phi)|Psi_kB> = (phi1-phi2)^2 [(4,2,0), Psi_0 G-norm 1]; -(theta12/2)(phi1-phi2)(phi1-phi3)(phi2-phi3) [(4,1,1), gnorm0 = 2]; -(theta12/2)(phi1-phi2)^3 [(3,3,0), gnorm0 = 2]; octet copy 1: -(5766(-3+Sqrt[5])/6125)(phi1-phi2)^2(phi1-phi3)(phi2-phi3) with gnorm0 = 1080(7-3Sqrt[5]), copy 2 conjugate; (961/4900)^2 ((phi1-phi2)(phi1-phi3)(phi2-phi3))^2 [(2,2,2), gnorm0 = 288]. Undo identity <Omega(w)(x)Omega(w')|h> = <phi_u(x)e1|h> verified exactly on every adjoint HW ket (eps = 1/1000, 3/7). The generating function: chat <phi_u (x) e1|Psi_B> = Sum_nu W_nu(phi,w1,w1') s[nu], W_nu = chat [e1 rho(n')]_nu polynomial in (w1,w1') (nu = 1..6, 8; W_7 has a simple pole 1/(w1'-phi2) but never carries a slice), s[nu] = Psi(nu,1) (exact: C_nu at order 0, exact linear/quadratic forms in phi at orders 1, 2 in the table); the polynomials Sum_nu C_nu W_nu for each branch are printed in section E5.\n\n**Data files** (`Paul/Mathematica/Gaudin/ref/untwisted-exact-<l1><l2><l3>.txt`, plain text, TAB-separated records, Wolfram InputForm, header lines starting with #): 110, 210, 220, 310, 320, 410. Records: REP, DIM, GTBASIS, WEIGHTS1, GMET1, THETA, NSECTORS, CAS1, SECTOR, HWBASIS (rational kets), GRAM, LAURMAT (theta12-scaled Laurent matrices), BRANCH (vector pair vA + Sqrt[D0] vB, exact G-norm^2 pair, CG slice pair, eta, alpha, beta pairs), XVEC (x(zeta)); the adjoint file additionally has E4_SERIES (phi and phi', orders 0..7, exact pairs), E4_SYMBOLIC (orders 0..3 strings in phi), E4_PSI, E4_GNORM, E5_KB, E5_SLICE, E5_GF.",
